.TH "HTMLTABLEELEMENT.TBODIES" "3JS" "August 19, 2026" "JavaScript" "JavaScript Reference Manual"
.SH NAME
HTMLTableElement.tBodies \- HTMLTableElement: tBodies property
.SH SYNOPSIS
The \f[B]\f[CB]tBodies\f[B]\f[R] read\-only property of the
\f[CR]HTMLTableElement\f[R] interface returns a live
\f[CR]HTMLCollection\f[R] of all \f[CR]<tbody>\f[R] element children of
the given \f[CR]<table>\f[R].
.PP
Although the property is read\-only, the returned object is live and is
automatically updated when the \f[CR]HTMLTableElement\f[R] changes.
.PP
The collection returned includes implicit \f[CR]<tbody>\f[R] elements.
For example:
.IP
.EX
<\f[B]table\f[R]>
  <\f[B]tr\f[R]>
    <\f[B]td\f[R]>cell one</\f[B]td\f[R]>
  </\f[B]tr\f[R]>
</\f[B]table\f[R]>
.EE
.PP
The HTML DOM generated from the above HTML will have a
\f[CR]<tbody>\f[R] element even though the tags are not included in the
source HTML.
.SH VALUE
A live \f[CR]HTMLCollection\f[R] of \f[CR]HTMLTableSectionElement\f[R]
(which are all \f[CR]tbody\f[R]) objects.
.SH EXAMPLES
This snippet gets the number of bodies in a table.
.IP
.EX
myTable.tBodies.length;
.EE
.SH SEE ALSO
.IP \(bu 2
\f[CR]HTMLTableElement.caption\f[R]
.IP \(bu 2
\f[CR]HTMLTableElement.tFoot\f[R]
.IP \(bu 2
